  "Notes": "Spacerless induced-transmission silver band-pass filter (calculated), thicker silver\nSpecification: Pass band peaked at 546 nm; stacks designed so Psi2 for h2 = 350 A is near its maximum and |cos(arg Y0)| ~ 1 at 546 nm\nReported: Fig. 9: half-width 2.4 deg phi; T < 0.05 % for phi = 69-78 deg and 102-111 deg (text p. 237); peak read from plot ~85 % (approximate).\nNotes: Ag 0.1282 x 546 = 70.0 nm. Same assumptions as Fig. 8 design.\nLayers from Text p. 235; Fig. 9 caption (h_Ag = 0.1282 lambda); layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nNot checked: the paper reports this design only as plots.",
